  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the retrieval:\n\n- **`pkg/registry/core/rest/storage_core.go`** \u2014 root of the error. `legacyProvider.PostStartHook()` registers the `\"start-service-ip-repair-controllers\"` hook, runs `startServiceClusterIPRepair` and `startServiceNodePortsRepair` concurrently via `async.Runner`, waits up to 1 minute on a `sync.WaitGroup`, and returns `errors.New(\"unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check\")` on timeout \u2014 this is the exact error in the ticket.\n- **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/controller/repairip.go`** \u2014 the `RepairIPAddress` controller (`NewRepairIPAddress`/`RunUntil`) used when `MultiCIDRServiceAllocator` is enabled (v1.33 default path). `RunUntil` blocks on informer cache sync and on the default `ServiceCIDR` object existing before calling `onFirstSuccess()` (the `wg.Done` that satisfies the PostStartHook's wait group).\n- **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/ipallocator.go`** \u2014 `Allocator.allocateService`/`allocateNextService` return `ErrNotReady` when `!a.ready.Load() || !a.ipAddressSynced()`; this is what surfaces as the `\"is forbidden: not yet ready to handle request\"` condition on `ipaddresses.networking.k8s.io` during the mixed-version window.\n- **`pkg/util/async/runner.go`** \u2014 the `Runner` primitive used to run both repair loops concurrently and fail together.\n- **`pkg/controlplane/instance.go`** \u2014 wires `RepairServicesInterval`/feature-gated construction and the default-ServiceCIDR post-start hook that the repair controller depends on.\n- **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/genericapiserver.go`** \u2014 generic PostStartHook/readyz machinery (`installReadyz`, `RunPostStartHooks`) that turns a hook failure into the `readyz` check failure reported (`poststarthook/start-service-ip-repair-controllers`).\n- **`pkg/registry/networking/ipaddress/strategy.go`**, **`staging/.../endpoints/handlers/create.go`** \u2014 the REST create path IPAddress objects go through, relevant to why creation requests get rejected while the allocator isn't ready.\n\nThe race: during a rolling upgrade, an old-version (v1.32) apiserver still using the legacy in-memory bitmap allocator races against the new v1.33 IPAddress-based repair controller, which requires the default `ServiceCIDR` object and informer caches to sync before `onFirstSuccess()` fires \u2014 under mixed-version load this can exceed the hardcoded 1-minute timeout, or the allocator is not marked ready before the readyz probe hits.",
